import pathlib,json,hashlib,shutil
P=pathlib.Path(__file__).parent
rows=[
('How are the King and home regions assigned, and where do each player’s initial ten Caballeros go?','Shuffle region cards; reveal top for King, each player takes another for home and places Grande. Two Caballeros home, one on first success-track space, seven court; remaining supply provinces.','2','Preparation'),
('Who begins playing power cards in the first and later rounds, in what seating direction do others play, and may a played value be matched?','Players choose first-round starter; previous round’s last player begins later rounds; clockwise; no duplicate value in a round.','3','Play the power cards'),
('What determines turn order and court recruitment, and when is recruitment done relative to choosing an action card?','Descending power value determines turns. Recruit at most pictured Caballeros from provinces into court first, then choose face-up action card.','3','Player turns'),
('If a power card allows recruitment but your provinces lack enough, what alternative is allowed, and which protected locations cannot supply it?','May remove own Caballeros from board to make up difference; not King’s region or Castillo (taboo and no Castillo removal outside general scoring).','3,4,7','Recruitment; taboo; Castillo'),
('Where may ordinary action-card deployment go, may it be split, and must the full printed allowance be used?','From court to regions adjacent to current King and/or Castillo; split freely; printed number is maximum, fewer allowed.','4,7','Deployment; E,F'),
('May special action and ordinary deployment be done in either order, may either be interleaved with the other, and may the special action be declined?','Either order, each completed wholly before next; no splitting/interleaving. Special action optional, may select card to prevent it.','3,7','Sequence; skipping'),
('What happens to selected and unselected face-up action cards after turns and rounds, and what is exceptional about the King card?','Chosen card laid aside unavailable to later players; remaining face-up cards discarded at round end; King card returns face-up every round, never permanently discarded.','4','Next Round'),
('What changes are forbidden in the King’s region, may it still be scored, and what kind of action changes its protected status?','No Caballeros, Grande or mobile scoreboard in/out, even special actions; scoring allowed. King-moving actions move King, changing which region is taboo.','4,7','King; A'),
('When putting Caballeros into the Castillo, what must be announced, how does King location affect entry, and when may they leave?','Announce number added; entry whenever adding/moving Caballeros regardless King; leave only at general scoring.','4,5,7','Castillo; C'),
('List the timing and ordered stages of general scoring, including when destinations are chosen relative to revealing the Castillo.','After rounds 3,6,9: secretly choose destinations first and place disks face down; uncover and score Castillo; reveal disks and move its Caballeros; score board regions in track order.','3,5','General scoring'),
('At general scoring, may one player split Castillo Caballeros between regions, choose the King’s region, or keep them in the Castillo; what happens if the King’s region was chosen?','All must go to single disk-selected region, not King’s region; Castillo emptied. Illegal King choice sends own Castillo Caballeros to own court.','5','Secret disk; move'),
('In a five-player scoring of 5/3/1, three players have four Caballeros each and another has three. What do these four players score, and do Grandes count?','Three tied leaders each 3 (second rank); next player third rank gets1. Grandes do not count toward majority.','5,6','Score Regions; example1'),
('In a five-player region worth 6/4/2 with counts 4,3,2,2, what does each score?','6,4,0,0: tied third players drop to fourth.','6','Example2'),
('Which scoreboard ranks pay in two-player and three-player games, and what happens to a two-player tie for first?','Two players only first rank; three only first two. Tied first drops to second so two-player tied leaders receive no points.','5','Score Regions'),
('When are the King’s and home bonuses awarded, how much is each, and what happens on a tied majority?','Whenever relevant region scored including special scoring; sole majority earns2 King bonus in King region and2 home bonus if own Grande there; neither for tied first.','6,10','Bonuses'),
('Does specially scoring the Castillo empty it or redistribute its Caballeros? Describe what happens.','Uncover and score; replace Castillo over same Caballeros; no redistribution until general scoring.','10,11','Special Castillo scoring'),
('Can a mobile scoreboard be put at the Castillo, moved into/out of King’s region, stacked on the other, or rotated to change its values?','Castillo allowed; King in/out prohibited; cannot stack; right side up only8/4/0 or4/0/0.','11','Mobile scoreboard'),
('What are the legal source/destination restrictions on moving your Grande, may other Grandes already be there, and what changes afterward?','Cannot leave King region or enter King region/Castillo; any other region even multiple Grandes; new region is home.','12','Grande'),
('Which power card may the recovery action return, can it be the card used this turn, and must the choice be revealed?','Any one played card, including current turn’s, to hand; need not reveal, though taking visible top is observable.','12','Power Cards'),
('When does the standard game end, and how is the winner determined?','After third general scoring following round9; furthest along success track/most points wins.','6','Game End')]
q={'game':'El Grande','scope':'1996 classic English base game pp.1–12; no expansions or optional short game','benchmark_version':'v1-seed','questions':[]};k={**{a:b for a,b in q.items() if a!='questions'},'answers':[]}
for i,(question,answer,page,section) in enumerate(rows,1):
 id=f'Q{i:02}';q['questions'].append({'id':id,'question':question});k['answers'].append({'id':id,'expected_answer':answer,'source_references':[{'path':'extracted/el-grande-rules.txt','pdf_pages':page,'section':section}]})
